---
# A no-provisioner class, so that D5 ("every PVC names its storage class explicitly") holds for
# a statically provisioned volume too, and so `kubectl get sc` says where media actually lives.
# Nothing provisions into this class — the single PV beside it is hand-declared.
#
# WaitForFirstConsumer is not a formality for a local volume: it makes the scheduler bind the
# claim only once it knows which node the consuming pod lands on, so a pod that cannot run on
# {{ inventory_hostname }} fails as Pending rather than binding first and mounting nothing.
apiVersion: storage.k8s.io/v1
kind: StorageClass
metadata:
  name: {{ media_volume_storage_class }}
provisioner: kubernetes.io/no-provisioner
volumeBindingMode: WaitForFirstConsumer
reclaimPolicy: Retain
